{
  "_note": "THE MOUNT-TABLE FOLD (studio-apps.md §8): resolveStudioApps(apps, state, opts) is PURE — discovered apps (each a kind: builtin | dev | installed, plus its validated manifest) + the consent state + the host options (denylist, verified approvals, the host's studioApi) fold into the mount table (rail · styleSections · inspectorSections · cards · tools · automations) and the REFUSALS, deterministically. The laws pinned here: a builtin/dev app with an enabled row mounts; a disabled row unmounts everything silently; an INSTALLED app without a consent row refuses loudly ('grants have not been reviewed'); an installed app without a verified approval refuses (the shelf signs coordinate/version/treeHash/grants — dev mode is how you run a working tree); an approval for a DIFFERENT version refuses; a denylisted scheme refuses with the recorded reason; a studioApi skew refuses per-app, typed, never a blank pane; an update that WIDENED grants beyond the recorded consent holds the whole app until re-consent (the panel renders the diff); rows order by (order, app, contribution id) so the rail is stable across machines. Each case's `apps` rows carry raw manifests — the runner validates through readAppManifest first, so this corpus also proves the fold consumes exactly what the grammar admits. Single-runner (the web Studio host — the spend-corpus standing). Runner: packages/cli/test/studio-apps-slots.test.ts.",
